The weekly view separates report arrival from merge time. Do not interpret its July merge spike
as a sudden increase in reports.

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

## Change triage, not just this ticket

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) is an accepted historical record.
Its subject-only rule conflicts with the rendered examples and is overdue for review under
the kb's half-year review rule. We preserve that record and replace its operational rule with
[decision 0002](/kb/decisions/0002-dedupe-by-cause).

Different subjects can share a cause. The same subject can hide different causes.
The same form channel can lead to different causes when tenants run different form versions.
An unknown tenant is unclassified: do not merge it just because its subject matches.

<DedupeExplorer />

## Desk procedure

1. Deduplicate export overlap by report ID.
2. Read the report and resolve its tenant locale, form version and channel.
3. Group only reports with the same supported cause. Keep unknown cases for investigation.
4. File separate engineering tickets and keep report membership, counts and examples with each.
5. Record each closure outcome and its evidence. Distinguish completed from not planned, and reported fixes from independent verification.
6. Rebuild these views when new desk exports arrive. Review this page after a change in the evidence.

## Evidence and limits

- Inputs: `src/lib/data/reports-4471.json`, `tenants/*.json` and `desk-notes.json`.
- Running classification: `src/lib/kb/causes.ts` and `locales.ts`.
- Report scope: the provided export only. Closure scope: the later course engineering update, checked 29 October. Neither supplies independent product-test evidence.
- The classification is a routing rule, not proof that every report body has the same root cause.
- Public engineering tickets: [parser](https://github.com/Hexrays/mega-s01e03/issues/1)
  and [form hint](https://github.com/Hexrays/mega-s01e03/issues/2).
- The source of this page is `src/routes/kb/incidents/4471-review/+page.svx`.
